Initiation)</h1>
<hr data-start=3D"252" data-end=3D"255">
<h2 data-start=3D"257" data-end=3D"284">1. Pourquoi Kubernetes ?</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"286" data-end=3D"312">1.1 Contexte et enjeux</h3>
<p data-start=3D"314" data-end=3D"597">Docker a r=C3=A9volutionn=C3=A9 la m=
ani=C3=A8re dont nous empaquetons et d=C3=A9ployons des applications gr=C3=
=A2ce aux conteneurs. Mais lorsqu=E2=80=99il s=E2=80=99agit de <strong data=
-start=3D"446" data-end=3D"504">g=C3=A9rer des applications conteneuris=C3=
=A9es =C3=A0 grande =C3=A9chelle</strong>, avec plusieurs instances r=C3=A9=
parties sur plusieurs machines, des besoins complexes =C3=A9mergent :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"599" data-end=3D"1128">
<li data-start=3D"599" data-end=3D"681">
<p data-start=3D"601" data-end=3D"681"><strong data-start=3D"601" data-end=
=3D"618">Orchestration</strong> : d=C3=A9marrer, arr=C3=AAter, red=C3=A9mar=
rer automatiquement les conteneurs</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"682" data-end=3D"757">
<p data-start=3D"684" data-end=3D"757"><strong data-start=3D"684" data-end=
=3D"711">Scalabilit=C3=A9 automatique</strong> : ajuster dynamiquement le n=
ombre d=E2=80=99instances</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"758" data-end=3D"836">
<p data-start=3D"760" data-end=3D"836"><strong data-start=3D"760" data-end=
=3D"781">Gestion du r=C3=A9seau</strong> : d=C3=A9couverte de services, rou=
tage, =C3=A9quilibre de charge</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"837" data-end=3D"906">
<p data-start=3D"839" data-end=3D"906"><strong data-start=3D"839" data-end=
=3D"862">Gestion du stockage</strong> : volumes partag=C3=A9s, persistance =
des donn=C3=A9es</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"907" data-end=3D"999">
<p data-start=3D"909" data-end=3D"999"><strong data-start=3D"909" data-end=
=3D"932">Haute disponibilit=C3=A9</strong> : assurer la r=C3=A9silience des=
 services malgr=C3=A9 les pannes mat=C3=A9rielles</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1000" data-end=3D"1077">
<p data-start=3D"1002" data-end=3D"1077"><strong data-start=3D"1002" data-e=
nd=3D"1025">D=C3=A9ploiement continu</strong> : mises =C3=A0 jour progressi=
ves et rollback automatique</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1078" data-end=3D"1128">
<p data-start=3D"1080" data-end=3D"1128"><strong data-start=3D"1080" data-e=
nd=3D"1092">S=C3=A9curit=C3=A9</strong> : gestion fine des acc=C3=A8s et se=
crets</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1130" data-end=3D"1320">Docker Swarm offre une solution si=
mple d=E2=80=99orchestration, mais quand les besoins deviennent plus comple=
xes et l=E2=80=99infrastructure plus large, <strong data-start=3D"1267" dat=
a-end=3D"1281">Kubernetes</strong> s=E2=80=99impose comme la plateforme sta=
ndard.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"1322" data-end=3D"1325">
<h3 data-start=3D"1327" data-end=3D"1361">1.2 Qu=E2=80=99est-ce que Kuberne=
tes ?</h3>
<p data-start=3D"1363" data-end=3D"1534">Kubernetes (abr=C3=A9g=C3=A9 k8s) =
est un syst=C3=A8me open-source d=E2=80=99orchestration de conteneurs d=C3=
=A9velopp=C3=A9 par Google, maintenant maintenu par la Cloud Native Computi=
ng Foundation (CNCF).</p>
<p data-start=3D"1536" data-end=3D"1701">Il permet de g=C3=A9rer des cluste=
rs de machines (physiques ou virtuelles) et de d=C3=A9ployer, g=C3=A9rer et=
 scaler des applications conteneuris=C3=A9es de fa=C3=A7on fiable et automa=
tis=C3=A9e.</p>
