<p data-start=3D"2835" data-end=3D"2946">Ce fichier demande =C3=A0 Kubernet=
es de toujours maintenir 3 Pods avec l=E2=80=99image NGINX, et de g=C3=A9re=
r leur cycle de vie.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"2948" data-end=3D"2951">
<h3 data-start=3D"2953" data-end=3D"3011">1.3 Service : abstraction r=C3=A9=
seau pour exposer les Pods</h3>
<p data-start=3D"3013" data-end=3D"3222"><strong data-start=3D"3013" data-e=
nd=3D"3029">D=C3=A9finition :</strong><br data-start=3D"3029" data-end=3D"3=
032">
Un <strong data-start=3D"3035" data-end=3D"3046">Service</strong> Kubernete=
s cr=C3=A9e une couche d=E2=80=99abstraction r=C3=A9seau qui expose un ou p=
lusieurs Pods en un point d=E2=80=99acc=C3=A8s stable (IP et/ou DNS), ind=
=C3=A9pendamment du cycle de vie des Pods individuels.</p>
<p data-start=3D"3224" data-end=3D"3351"><strong data-start=3D"3224" data-e=
nd=3D"3249">Pourquoi un Service ?</strong><br data-start=3D"3249" data-end=
=3D"3252">
Les Pods peuvent =C3=AAtre d=C3=A9truits et recr=C3=A9=C3=A9s, ce qui modif=
ie leur adresse IP. Le Service permet donc :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"3353" data-end=3D"3563">
<li data-start=3D"3353" data-end=3D"3414">
<p data-start=3D"3355" data-end=3D"3414">Une <strong data-start=3D"3359" da=
ta-end=3D"3380">adresse IP stable</strong> (ClusterIP) pour acc=C3=A9der au=
x Pods</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3415" data-end=3D"3470">
<p data-start=3D"3417" data-end=3D"3470">Un <strong data-start=3D"3420" dat=
a-end=3D"3438">load balancing</strong> entre plusieurs Pods (r=C3=A9plicas)=
</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3471" data-end=3D"3563">
<p data-start=3D"3473" data-end=3D"3563">Une exposition du service =C3=A0 l=
=E2=80=99ext=C3=A9rieur du cluster (via NodePort, LoadBalancer ou Ingress)<=
/p>
</li>
</ul>
