<hr data-start=3D"2090" data-end=3D"2093">
<h4 data-start=3D"2095" data-end=3D"2135">2.2.2 Outils externes de monitori=
ng</h4>
<ul data-start=3D"2137" data-end=3D"2547">
<li data-start=3D"2137" data-end=3D"2303">
<p data-start=3D"2139" data-end=3D"2303"><strong data-start=3D"2139" data-e=
nd=3D"2151">cAdvisor</strong> (Container Advisor) :<br data-start=3D"2173" =
data-end=3D"2176">
Outil d=C3=A9velopp=C3=A9 par Google, collecte des m=C3=A9triques d=C3=A9ta=
ill=C3=A9es sur les performances des conteneurs et fournit une interface we=
b.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2305" data-end=3D"2456">
<p data-start=3D"2307" data-end=3D"2456"><strong data-start=3D"2307" data-e=
nd=3D"2331">Prometheus + Grafana</strong> :<br data-start=3D"2333" data-end=
=3D"2336">
Prometheus collecte les m=C3=A9triques (CPU, RAM, r=C3=A9seau=E2=80=A6), Gr=
afana les affiche sous forme de tableaux de bord personnalis=C3=A9s.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2458" data-end=3D"2547">
<p data-start=3D"2460" data-end=3D"2547"><strong data-start=3D"2460" data-e=
nd=3D"2478">Sysdig / Falco</strong> :<br data-start=3D"2480" data-end=3D"24=
83">
Outils avanc=C3=A9s pour le monitoring et la s=C3=A9curit=C3=A9 des contene=
urs.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"2549" data-end=3D"2552">
<h3 data-start=3D"2554" data-end=3D"2591">2.3 Comprendre les m=C3=A9triques=
 cl=C3=A9s</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"2593" data-end=3D"3040">
<li data-start=3D"2593" data-end=3D"2716">
<p data-start=3D"2595" data-end=3D"2716"><strong data-start=3D"2595" data-e=
nd=3D"2608">CPU usage</strong> :<br data-start=3D"2610" data-end=3D"2613">
Mesure la charge CPU consomm=C3=A9e. Attention aux pics d=E2=80=99utilisati=
on pouvant provoquer des ralentissements.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2718" data-end=3D"2832">
<p data-start=3D"2720" data-end=3D"2832"><strong data-start=3D"2720" data-e=
nd=3D"2736">Memory usage</strong> :<br data-start=3D"2738" data-end=3D"2741=
">
S=E2=80=99assurer que la m=C3=A9moire consomm=C3=A9e ne d=C3=A9passe pas la=
 limite (=C3=A9viter le swap ou OOM Killer).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2834" data-end=3D"2952">
<p data-start=3D"2836" data-end=3D"2952"><strong data-start=3D"2836" data-e=
nd=3D"2847">IO disk</strong> :<br data-start=3D"2849" data-end=3D"2852">
Le d=C3=A9bit d=E2=80=99=C3=A9criture et lecture sur disque impacte les per=
formances des bases de donn=C3=A9es ou fichiers.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"2954" data-end=3D"3040">
<p data-start=3D"2956" data-end=3D"3040"><strong data-start=3D"2956" data-e=
nd=3D"2970">Network IO</strong> :<br data-start=3D"2972" data-end=3D"2975">
Important pour les services d=C3=A9pendants des communications r=C3=A9seau.=
</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3042" data-end=3D"3045">
<h3 data-start=3D"3047" data-end=3D"3081">2.4 Optimiser les performances</h=
3>
<ul data-start=3D"3083" data-end=3D"3541">
<li data-start=3D"3083" data-end=3D"3208">
<p data-start=3D"3085" data-end=3D"3208">Configurer des <strong data-start=
=3D"3100" data-end=3D"3126">limites CPU et m=C3=A9moire</strong> dans le fi=
chier Docker ou au moment du <code data-start=3D"3166" data-end=3D"3178">do=
cker run</code> (flags <code data-start=3D"3186" data-end=3D"3196">--memory=
</code>, <code data-start=3D"3198" data-end=3D"3206">--cpus</code>).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3210" data-end=3D"3308">
<p data-start=3D"3212" data-end=3D"3308">Utiliser des <strong data-start=3D=
"3225" data-end=3D"3246">volumes optimis=C3=A9s</strong> pour r=C3=A9duire =
les ralentissements li=C3=A9s =C3=A0 l=E2=80=99acc=C3=A8s aux fichiers.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3310" data-end=3D"3427">
<p data-start=3D"3312" data-end=3D"3427">Favoriser des images l=C3=A9g=C3=
=A8res et minimales (ex : Alpine) pour diminuer le temps de d=C3=A9marrage =
et l=E2=80=99empreinte m=C3=A9moire.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"3429" data-end=3D"3541">
<p data-start=3D"3431" data-end=3D"3541">Mettre en place une <strong data-s=
tart=3D"3451" data-end=3D"3478">scalabilit=C3=A9 horizontale</strong> via o=
rchestrateur (Kubernetes, Swarm) pour r=C3=A9partir la charge.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"3543" data-end=3D"3546">
<h2 data-start=3D"3548" data-end=3D"3582">3. Patterns avanc=C3=A9s dans Doc=
ker</h2>
<p data-start=3D"3584" data-end=3D"3783">Dans des architectures complexes, =
des patterns sp=C3=A9cifiques =C3=A9mergent pour r=C3=A9soudre des probl=C3=
=A9matiques fr=C3=A9quentes comme la gestion de la configuration, la s=C3=
=A9curisation, la gestion du cycle de vie, etc.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"3785" data-end=3D"3788">
<h3 data-start=3D"3790" data-end=3D"3813">3.1 Sidecar pattern</h3>
<h4 data-start=3D"3815" data-end=3D"3830">D=C3=A9finition</h4>
<p data-start=3D"3832" data-end=3D"4088">Le pattern <strong data-start=3D"3=
843" data-end=3D"3854">Sidecar</strong> consiste =C3=A0 ex=C3=A9cuter un co=
nteneur auxiliaire =C3=A0 c=C3=B4t=C3=A9 du conteneur principal dans un m=
=C3=AAme Pod (Kubernetes) ou dans le m=C3=AAme contexte de service. Ce side=
car apporte des fonctionnalit=C3=A9s compl=C3=A9mentaires sans alourdir le =
conteneur principal.</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"4090" data-end=3D"4115">Cas d=E2=80=99usage typiques</h4>
<ul data-start=3D"4117" data-end=3D"4231">
<li data-start=3D"4117" data-end=3D"4150">
<p data-start=3D"4119" data-end=3D"4150">Collecte de logs (ex : Fluentd)</p=
>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4151" data-end=3D"4178">
<p data-start=3D"4153" data-end=3D"4178">Proxy r=C3=A9seau (ex : Envoy)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4179" data-end=3D"4201">
<p data-start=3D"4181" data-end=3D"4201">Mise en cache locale</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4202" data-end=3D"4231">
<p data-start=3D"4204" data-end=3D"4231">Synchronisation de fichiers</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h4 data-start=3D"4233" data-end=3D"4245">Exemple</h4>
<p data-start=3D"4247" data-end=3D"4349">Un service web avec un sidecar Flu=
entd qui collecte les logs et les envoie vers un syst=C3=A8me centralis=C3=
