<p data-start=3D"5854" data-end=3D"5935">Le conteneur principal <code data-=
start=3D"5877" data-end=3D"5887">main-app</code> ne d=C3=A9marre qu=E2=80=
=99apr=C3=A8s la fin de l=E2=80=99init-container.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"5937" data-end=3D"5940">
<h2 data-start=3D"5942" data-end=3D"5990">4. Mise en pratique : cas r=C3=A9=
els d=E2=80=99utilisation</h2>
<h3 data-start=3D"5992" data-end=3D"6042">4.1 Monitoring de la performance =
en production</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"6044" data-end=3D"6289">
<li data-start=3D"6044" data-end=3D"6125">
<p data-start=3D"6046" data-end=3D"6125">D=C3=A9ployer cAdvisor ou int=C3=
=A9grer Prometheus/Grafana pour surveiller en temps r=C3=A9el.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6126" data-end=3D"6207">
<p data-start=3D"6128" data-end=3D"6207">D=C3=A9finir des alertes sur les m=
=C3=A9triques critiques (ex : CPU &gt; 80% sur 5 minutes).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6208" data-end=3D"6289">
<p data-start=3D"6210" data-end=3D"6289">Analyser r=C3=A9guli=C3=A8rement l=
es rapports pour identifier les conteneurs =C3=A0 optimiser.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"6291" data-end=3D"6352">4.2 Architecture microservices av=
ec Sidecar et Ambassador</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"6354" data-end=3D"6532">
<li data-start=3D"6354" data-end=3D"6446">
<p data-start=3D"6356" data-end=3D"6446">Chaque microservice s=E2=80=99acco=
mpagne d=E2=80=99un sidecar pour la collecte des logs ou gestion r=C3=A9sea=
u.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6447" data-end=3D"6532">
<p data-start=3D"6449" data-end=3D"6532">Un ambassador g=C3=A8re la communi=
cation s=C3=A9curis=C3=A9e vers des services critiques externes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"6534" data-end=3D"6586">4.3 Initialisation complexe avec =
init-containers</h3>
<ul data-start=3D"6588" data-end=3D"6741">
<li data-start=3D"6588" data-end=3D"6669">
<p data-start=3D"6590" data-end=3D"6669">Lors du d=C3=A9ploiement, un init-=
container lance les migrations de base de donn=C3=A9es.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6670" data-end=3D"6741">
<p data-start=3D"6672" data-end=3D"6741">Puis, le conteneur principal d=C3=
=A9marre uniquement si la base est pr=C3=AAte.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<hr data-start=3D"6743" data-end=3D"6746">
<h2 data-start=3D"6748" data-end=3D"6764">5. Conclusion</h2>
<p data-start=3D"6766" data-end=3D"6818">Docker en production n=C3=A9cessit=
e une approche mature :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"6820" data-end=3D"7207">
<li data-start=3D"6820" data-end=3D"6926">
<p data-start=3D"6822" data-end=3D"6926"><strong data-start=3D"6822" data-e=
nd=3D"6847">Analyser et monitorer</strong> r=C3=A9guli=C3=A8rement les perf=
ormances est indispensable pour anticiper les probl=C3=A8mes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6927" data-end=3D"7060">
<p data-start=3D"6929" data-end=3D"7060">Les <strong data-start=3D"6933" da=
ta-end=3D"6953">patterns avanc=C3=A9s</strong> (sidecar, ambassador, init-c=
ontainer) offrent des solutions =C3=A9l=C3=A9gantes et modulaires aux besoi=
ns complexes.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7061" data-end=3D"7207">
<p data-start=3D"7063" data-end=3D"7207">Ces techniques sont souvent combin=
=C3=A9es dans des environnements orchestr=C3=A9s comme Kubernetes pour gara=
ntir robustesse, flexibilit=C3=A9, et scalabilit=C3=A9.</p>
</li>
</ul>
