<hr data-start=3D"6202" data-end=3D"6205">
<h2 data-start=3D"6207" data-end=3D"6273">5. Bonnes pratiques et recommanda=
tions pour le debugging Docker</h2>
<ul data-start=3D"6275" data-end=3D"6958">
<li data-start=3D"6275" data-end=3D"6385">
<p data-start=3D"6277" data-end=3D"6385"><strong data-start=3D"6277" data-e=
nd=3D"6384">Privil=C3=A9gier les logs et acc=C3=A8s shell (<code data-start=
=3D"6316" data-end=3D"6329">docker logs</code>, <code data-start=3D"6331" d=
ata-end=3D"6344">docker exec</code>) avant d=E2=80=99aller vers les outils =
lourds</strong>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6386" data-end=3D"6531">
<p data-start=3D"6388" data-end=3D"6531">Pour diagnostiquer la configuratio=
n r=C3=A9seau, utiliser <code data-start=3D"6441" data-end=3D"6465">docker =
network inspect</code> et des outils comme <code data-start=3D"6486" data-e=
nd=3D"6492">ping</code>, <code data-start=3D"6494" data-end=3D"6500">curl</=
code>, <code data-start=3D"6502" data-end=3D"6512">nslookup</code> dans le =
conteneur.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6532" data-end=3D"6603">
<p data-start=3D"6534" data-end=3D"6603">Utiliser <code data-start=3D"6543"=
 data-end=3D"6557">docker stats</code> r=C3=A9guli=C3=A8rement pour surveil=
ler les ressources.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6604" data-end=3D"6687">
<p data-start=3D"6606" data-end=3D"6687">Isoler les probl=C3=A8mes en lan=
=C3=A7ant des conteneurs minimaux et tester les hypoth=C3=A8ses.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6688" data-end=3D"6866">
<p data-start=3D"6690" data-end=3D"6866">Pour debug plus profond, installer=
 temporairement des outils comme <code data-start=3D"6757" data-end=3D"6765=
">strace</code>, <code data-start=3D"6767" data-end=3D"6776">tcpdump</code>=
 dans l=E2=80=99image ou utiliser des images debug d=C3=A9di=C3=A9es (<code=
 data-start=3D"6828" data-end=3D"6837">busybox</code>, <code data-start=3D"=
6839" data-end=3D"6847">alpine</code> avec utilitaires).</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6867" data-end=3D"6958">
<p data-start=3D"6869" data-end=3D"6958">Automatiser la collecte des logs e=
t metrics via des solutions externes (ELK, Prometheus).</p>
</li>
</ul>
